{{also|stossen|Stößen}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|stossen}} {{q|Switzerland and Liechtenstein}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|stōzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stōzan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*stautan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stautaną}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro||*stówd-e-ti}}, an o-grade intensive formation from {{m|ine-pro|*(s)tewd-||to hit, push}}. 

Akin to {{cog|non|stauta}} and {{m|non|steyta}} (whence {{cog|da|støde}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌿𐍄𐌰𐌽}}. Non-Germanic cognates include {{cog|la|tundo}}. Compare {{cog|sa|तुदति|tr=tudáti||to strike, goad}}, {{m|sa|तोद|tr=todá||driver, impeller}}. Related to {{cog|nl|stoten||to push, bump}} and {{cog|en|stot||to bounce, rebound, ricochet, or make bounce, rebound or ricochet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtoːsən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-stoßen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|stoßen<stößt#stieß,gestoßen.haben,sein>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[push]]; to [[shove]]; to [[thrust]] {{i|conjugated with {{m|de|haben}}}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|reflexive}} to [[bump]]; to [[knock]]; to [[strike]]; to [[hurt]] {{i|conjugated with {{m|de|haben}}}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|figuratively|with ''[[an#German|an]]''}} to [[take exception]] (to something) {{i|conjugated with {{m|de|haben}}}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[jolt]]; to [[kick]]; to [[thrust]] {{i|conjugated with {{m|de|haben}}}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with ''[[an#German|an]]'' or ''[[gegen]]''}} to [[bump]] (into something); to [[knock]] (against something) {{i|conjugated with {{m|de|sein}}}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with ''[[auf]]''}} to [[come]] (across something); to [[happen]] (upon something); to [[stumble]] (upon something) {{i|conjugated with {{m|de|sein}}}}

